    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8241",
      "problem": "Let $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function $f(x)$ shown below. What is the mode of $X?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/137e06758f63232479a573ffd7c7c68cffd832d8fac22036bce04e9968ad7c4a.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The mode of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ is the value of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that $f(x)$ has a single global maximum at $x=7.$\n\nTherefore, the mode of $X$ is $7.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/d500063d0885dc2437d83754d8e54d81740a8b6fd1855416e51dab2577cb27a6.png)",
